                <pb facs="0964" n="884" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg884"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Merry to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-06-20"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 20, 1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 734.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to advise the receipt of a
                    telegram dated this day from the Hon. Fernando Sanchez, minister of foreign
                    relations of the Republic of Nicaragua, informing me that his Government will be
                    pleased to permit consular officers of the United States to use their good
                    offices on behalf of the citizens of the Republic of Cuba resident in or
                    visiting Nicaragua. Of this I have advised United States consuls in Nicaragua in
                    accordance with your instructions.</p>
                <p>With assurances, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Lawrence
                    Merry.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
